<h2 id="includes">What This Service Includes</h2>
<p>Implementation is the bridge between a decision to offer regenerative medicine and a program that runs reliably. We design the workflows, put the standardized protocol in place, and train the people who deliver it — then standardize the whole thing so it doesn't depend on any one person.</p>

<h3>What We Put In Place</h3>
<div class="dash-list">
  <div class="dash-list-item">Workflow design mapped to your rooms, staff roles, and chair time</div>
  <div class="dash-list-item">The one consistent, ultrasound-guided clinical protocol</div>
  <div class="dash-list-item">Staff onboarding and competency training, with sign-off records</div>
  <div class="dash-list-item">Operational standardization so the program runs the same way every time</div>
</div>

<h2 id="protocol">One Consistent Protocol</h2>
<p>Everything is built around a single standardized protocol — the same preparation and technique on every case, with ultrasound guidance placing the injection precisely at the site of injury rather than by surface landmarks. Consistent inputs are what make outcomes, and the documentation behind them, consistent. That's the opposite of a bedside kit and a technique that lives in one person's head.</p>

<h2 id="training">Training to Competency</h2>
<p>Your whole team is trained in person — providers plus front- and back-office staff — by board-certified physicians in pain medicine and musculoskeletal ultrasound. Timing is individualized to your practice.</p>

<div class="numbered-steps">
  <div class="numbered-step">
    <span class="numbered-step-badge">1</span>
    <div>
      <div class="numbered-step-title">In-Person Training</div>
      <p class="numbered-step-body">Training happens on-site, in your own procedure rooms and on your own equipment — not remotely.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="numbered-step">
    <span class="numbered-step-badge">2</span>
    <div>
      <div class="numbered-step-title">Live Proctoring</div>
      <p class="numbered-step-body">Your first cases are proctored live, so the team learns the protocol on real cases with support in the room.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="numbered-step">
    <span class="numbered-step-badge">3</span>
    <div>
      <div class="numbered-step-title">Sign-Off &amp; Ongoing Support</div>
      <p class="numbered-step-body">Staff are signed off to competency on the record, and Regenitiva stays involved for future training as the program grows.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="callout">
  <div class="callout-label">Why this matters</div>
  <p class="callout-body">A program that only one person knows how to run isn't a program — it's a dependency. Standardized workflows and documented competency mean the protocol runs the same whether or not any single team member is there that day.</p>
</div>

